{"id":3,"question":"Which statement best describes the 'Place Value' of a digit?","right_answer":"A digit's value comes from its place, not from the digit alone.","feedback_for_wrong_option":"The value of a digit depends on how many times it appears in a number.","kind":"wrong","text":"The number of times a digit appears does not change its 'Place Value'. For example, in 9999, each 9 has a different 'Place Value' because of its position, even though it's the same digit 9.","words_now":35,"max_words":18}

